<p>The insurance estimate is the document that drives your settlement, yet most property owners receive it with little explanation. Pages of line items, abbreviations, unit prices, and depreciation columns can make it hard to tell whether the estimate actually matches the damage. An <strong>insurance estimate review in San Antonio</strong> walks through that document line by line, comparing it with what is on your roof, walls, and floors, so you understand what is included, what may be missing, and how the final number was reached. Sometimes a review confirms the estimate is reasonable. Often it turns up items worth raising with the insurer.</p>

<h2>What We Look At in a Line-by-Line Xactimate Review</h2>
<p>Most insurers write estimates in Xactimate. Each line has a description, a quantity, a unit price, tax, and often depreciation. A careful review looks at each part.</p>
<table>
<thead><tr><th>Area</th><th>Questions we ask</th></tr></thead>
<tbody>
<tr><td>Scope</td><td>Is every damaged component included? Are rooms, elevations, or structures missing?</td></tr>
<tr><td>Repair vs. replace</td><td>Does the estimate repair items that cannot reasonably be repaired or matched?</td></tr>
<tr><td>Quantities</td><td>Do roof squares, waste, wall and ceiling square footage, and linear feet match the measurements?</td></tr>
<tr><td>Line item selection</td><td>Does each code describe the actual material and method, or a cheaper substitute?</td></tr>
<tr><td>Pricing</td><td>Is the price list for the San Antonio area and the correct time period?</td></tr>
<tr><td>Code and permit items</td><td>Are permit fees and code-required items included where ordinance or law coverage applies?</td></tr>
<tr><td>Overhead and profit</td><td>Does the job reasonably require a general contractor to coordinate several trades?</td></tr>
<tr><td>Depreciation</td><td>Is depreciation reasonable for the age and condition? Is it recoverable under the policy?</td></tr>
<tr><td>Deductible and prior payments</td><td>Is the correct deductible applied, and are prior payments accounted for?</td></tr>
</tbody>
</table>

